;; Denies IP networking to a process tree while leaving everything else alone.
;;
;; What this proves: that Poptart's Dictation, history, settings, and model execution complete with
;; every outbound, inbound, and bound IP socket refused by the kernel. It is a capability proof about
;; one process tree, not a statement about the shipping product: the bundle under test is ad-hoc
;; signed rather than notarized, and a sandbox says nothing about code that never ran. The clean
;; install traffic capture in traffic_capture.sh is the observation proof that complements it.
;;
;; A plain (deny network*) also refuses AF_UNIX connects, which is how processes reach syslogd,
;; the pasteboard server, and the window server, so the app dies at launch and the run proves
;; nothing. AF_UNIX connects arrive as network-outbound carrying a filesystem path, so the socket
;; directories system services listen in are allowed back.
(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny network-outbound)
(deny network-inbound)
(deny network-bind)
(allow network-outbound (regex #"^/private/var/run/" #"^/var/run/" #"^/private/tmp/"))
